  <Docs>
    <summary>
            Options for verifying a signature with a post-quantum ML-DSA (AKP) key using
            <see cref="M:Azure.Security.KeyVault.Keys.Cryptography.CryptographyClient.Verify(Azure.Security.KeyVault.Keys.Cryptography.MLDsaVerifyOptions,System.Threading.CancellationToken)" />.
            </summary>
    <remarks>
      <see cref="P:Azure.Security.KeyVault.Keys.Cryptography.MLDsaVerifyOptions.Signature" /> is always required. Exactly one of <see cref="P:Azure.Security.KeyVault.Keys.Cryptography.MLDsaVerifyOptions.Message" /> or
            <see cref="P:Azure.Security.KeyVault.Keys.Cryptography.MLDsaVerifyOptions.ExternalMu" /> must be set. When <see cref="P:Azure.Security.KeyVault.Keys.Cryptography.MLDsaVerifyOptions.ExternalMu" /> is specified,
            <see cref="P:Azure.Security.KeyVault.Keys.Cryptography.MLDsaVerifyOptions.Context" /> must not be set. The algorithm is inferred from the key and is not
            specified by the caller.
            </remarks>
  </Docs>
